/E (M1, the Crab Nebula, is a supernova remnant in Taurus, located about 6,500 light-years away. It formed from a supernova recorded in 1054 CE and spans 11 light-years. At its core is the Crab Pulsar, a rapidly spinning neutron star emitting intense radiation. This nebula is a rich mix of ionized gas and high-energy radiation, making it a key target for studying stellar death and astrophysics. Visible through telescopes, it's best observed during winter.)
